group_by() + summarize()

covid |&gt;
  group_by(drive_thru_ind) |&gt;
  summarize(
    n_tests      = n(),
    pct_positive = mean(result == "positive") * 100
  )

# A tibble: 2 × 3
  drive_thru_ind n_tests pct_positive
           &lt;int&gt;   &lt;int&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;
1              0    7537         5.12
2              1    7987         6.00



One row per group. This is the workhorse of descriptive epidemiology.

A full pipeline
Positivity by gender among patients, excluding invalid tests:

covid |&gt;
  filter(demo_group == "patient", result != "invalid") |&gt;
  group_by(gender) |&gt;
  summarize(
    n = n(),
    pct_positive = round(mean(result == "positive") * 100, 1)
  )

# A tibble: 2 × 3
  gender     n pct_positive
  &lt;chr&gt;  &lt;int&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;
1 female  6082          4.9
2 male    5969          4.2

Part 5: Put it all together

Exercise 9
Among patients only, and excluding invalid tests, what percent of tests were positive for each gender? Round pct_positive to 1 decimal place.









Two conditions in filter(): demo_group == "patient" and result != "invalid" (!= means “not equal to”).


For the percent, reuse mean(result == "positive") * 100 from Exercise 7.


covid |&gt;
  filter(demo_group == "patient", result != "invalid") |&gt;
  group_by(gender) |&gt;
  summarize(
    n = n(),
    pct_positive = round(mean(result == "positive") * 100, 1)
  )
